{"base_manifest_sha256":"531f85386978d805de3756d2d1c70d748a4cd392c0caad3c4173e8a9d9c6fa06","review":{"basis":"Pending entries use a bounded historical OHLC model; incomplete v1-v2 signatures are reconstructed and intrabar activation never implies a known tick path.","date":"2026-10-24","decisions":["v1 has entry names without signatures; v2 has stop examples but incomplete limit/stop-limit shapes. Those gaps are reconstructed explicitly. v3-v6 expose limit and stop; when is admitted only through v5.","A named limit or stop opts the program into persistent entries and the shared partial-exit accounting engine. Both na choose market; other programs preserve their old broker profiles.","Entries are first eligible on the next bar. Limits improve at an eligible open or fill at a touched level without slippage. Stops cross at open or touch at the level with adverse pinned slippage. Quantity is positive, fixed and step-aligned; volume does not split entry fills.","Stop-limit is a two-stage order. Activation at open permits the limit on that bar; activation on an unknown intrabar touch defers the limit to the next bar, even if it could already be marketable. No interpolated tick path or future-price ordering is claimed.","All known open executions use sequence order. Existing and open-activated protection precedes conditional intrabar entries. At most one actual intrabar entry fill is admitted per bar; other eligible entries remain pending with a reason. Protection attached to an intrabar fill first executes next bar.","Same entry ID replaces its exact pending order, resets stop-limit activation and cancels protection attached to the old order. cancel/cancel_all remove pending entries and attached reservations. Missing-target closes are ignored; they do not cancel unfilled entries.","One position, no pyramiding, no expiry, no custom OCA groups, trailing, volume partial fills or observed/live protective execution. Full-close/reversal and partial-exit fees use the separately 